      "message": "In https://aomedia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/aom/+/200541 we started to compile libaom\u0027s C++ code with the `-std\u003dc++17` flag. Apparently our `-std\u003dc++17` flag is overridden by Android NDK r25 so that the actual C++ standard enabled is older than C++17. See the Android compilation errors in https://build.aomedia.org/jenkins/job/libaom__compile/62762/\n\nPossible solutions I found on the Web include setting the `CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD` variable (which affects all targets) and setting the `CXX_STANDARD` property of a target, but I like this solution the best because it also causes the clients of `aom_gtest` to use C++17.",
